# Secrets and local environment
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p8

# Rust build output
/target/

# Measurement harnesses, which build a throwaway integration test by copying a
# real one and appending to the copy. They used to append to the tracked file
# and revert it afterwards; a background run and a `git add -A` then put two
# hundred lines of scratch into a commit. Cargo discovers anything matching
# tests/*.rs, so the copy runs without being registered anywhere -- and being
# ignored here is what keeps it out of a commit by construction rather than by
# remembering. The harnesses delete these on the way in as well as on the way
# out, because a run that is killed never reaches its trap.
crates/*/tests/scratch_*.rs

# Python bytecode, from running the budget script
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Rust local/editor outputs
**/*.rs.bk

